Vous, je fais quoi ? Je vous offre un verre ?
What do I do for you? Get you a drink?

101
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,430
Il prendra quoi, votre ami ?
What will your friend have?

102
00:02:14,430 --> 00:02:15,110
À lui ?
Him?

103
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:16,030
10 %.
Ten percent.

104
00:03:07,450 --> 00:03:08,590
C'est bon, il a confirmé.
Good, he confirmed.

105
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,210
Rendez-vous dans une demi-heure à Belleville.
Meet in half an hour in Belleville.

106
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:10,890
OK, super.
OK, great.

107
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:11,920
Tu pars en premier.
You go first.

108
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:12,800
Moi, je te suis en secondaire.
I'll follow behind.

109
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:23,760
Surtout, fais profil bas avec Hicham.
Most importantly, keep a low profile with Hicham.

110
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:24,680
C'est le contraire.
It's the opposite.

111
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,520
Si je suis sympa avec lui, c'est ça qui va le rendre parano.
If I'm nice to him, that's what's going to make him paranoid.

112
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,200
Il va se douter qu'il y a énormément d'intérêt à ce que je dis.
He'll suspect there's a lot riding on what I'm saying.

113
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:29,340
Ça va ? On parle de moi ?
You good? You talking about me?

114
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:31,870
Non, non, non.
No, no, no.

115
00:03:32,050 --> 00:03:33,830
Tout ne tourne pas autour de ton nom, Moïse.
Not everything revolves around your name, Moïse.

116
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,500
Ça va ? Tu fais quoi ? Tu fais une pause ?
You good? What are you doing? Taking a break?

117
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:41,310
Non, pas du tout.
No, not at all.

118
00:03:41,390 --> 00:03:41,850
Ce n'est pas mon genre.
Not my style.

119
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:43,030
Je me réhydrate.
Just rehydrating.

120
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:46,300
Et je retourne bosser.
Then I'm getting back to work.

121
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:48,260
Voilà, je cours, je vole.
Here we go, I'm running, I'm flying.

122
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:49,300
Hop, hop, hop, hop, hop, hop.
Hop, hop, hop, hop, hop, hop.

123
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:50,410
Tu sais quoi ? Je t'accompagne.
You know what? I'll come with you.

124
00:03:50,690 --> 00:03:51,450
Quoi, tout ça ?
What, all that?

125
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:51,930
Bosser.
Work.

126
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:53,330
On va voir quelques techniques de négo.
We're going to look at some negotiation techniques.

127
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,190
Tu es trop passif dans les échanges.
You're too passive in exchanges.

128
00:03:55,310 --> 00:03:56,050
Trop en réaction.
Too reactive.

129
00:03:56,050 --> 00:04:02,210
Mais non, ce n'est pas possible parce que j'ai prévu d'aller chez le dentiste.
No, that's not possible, I've got a dentist appointment.

130
00:04:02,690 --> 00:04:08,990
On peut bosser, tu vois, mais après ? Et crois-moi, je te jure, je préférais largement
We can work, sure, but after? And trust me, I swear, I'd much rather

131
00:04:08,990 --> 00:04:09,830
passer la matinée avec toi.
spend the morning with you.

132
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,100
Désolé de vous avoir donné rendez-vous ici, Maitre Hirsch.
Sorry for meeting you here, Maître Hirsch.

133
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,540
Oui, on voulait rester discret.
Yes, we wanted to keep a low profile.

134
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:20,120
Mais au moins, ici, on est sûr de ne croiser personne du métier.
But at least here, we're sure not to run into anyone from the business.

135
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,080
Oui, j'avais compris.
Yes, I'd gathered that.

136
00:04:22,370 --> 00:04:24,490
Donc, pour votre affaire, vous êtes pressé ?
So, for your matter — are you in a hurry?

137
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:27,890
Idéalement, il faudrait que la nouvelle structure soit prête avant que j'accouche.
Ideally, the new structure should be ready before I give birth.

138
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:30,430
Donc, d'ici trois semaines, un mois.
So, within three weeks, a month.

139
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:36,740
Ça vous paraît jouable ? C'est pas large, mais on n'a plus mal.
Does that seem doable? It's tight, but we're not in pain anymore.

140
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:40,700
Quand on veut quitter sa boîte, surtout pour monter une agence concurrente, on veut faire
When you want to leave your firm, especially to set up a competing agency, you want to move

141
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:40,920
vite.
fast.

142
00:04:42,210 --> 00:04:43,530
Vous n'avez parlé à personne ?
You haven't spoken to anyone?

143
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:44,450
Non, bien sûr que non.
No, of course not.

144
00:04:44,970 --> 00:04:46,790
On pourrait informer nos talents, non ?
Could we inform our talent?

145
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:48,800
Le plus tard possible.
As late as possible.

146
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:52,120
Donc, concrètement, qu'est-ce qu'on risque ?
So, concretely, what are we risking?

147
00:04:53,150 --> 00:04:59,050
Il ne faut pas que vos deux chiffres d'affaires cumulés atteignent 50 % de celui de la société.
Your two combined turnovers must not reach 50% of the company's.

148
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,890
Parce que sinon, vous portez atteinte à l'intégrité d'ASK.
Because otherwise, you're undermining ASK's integrity.

149
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:03,590
Ça s'appelle du démantèlement.
That's called asset stripping.

150
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:06,210
Et ça, c'est un verdict.
And that carries a verdict.

151
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:08,390
Alors, regardez, justement.
So, look, right here.

152
00:05:09,590 --> 00:05:11,870
Voilà, ça, c'est les chiffres d'ASK.
This is ASK's figures.

153
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:14,780
Et voilà nos chiffres.
And these are our figures.

154
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:17,680
On est bons, non ?
We're good, right?

155
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,500
C'est juste.
That's correct.

156
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:26,830
Moi, je vous recommande vivement de ne rentrer surtout aucun nouveau contrat jusqu'à votre départ.
I strongly advise you not to take on any new contracts before you leave.

157
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:31,070
Ça vous paraît possible ?
Does that seem possible?

158
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:32,430
Oui, ça, c'est dans mes cornes.
Yes, that's within my scope.

159
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,340
Oui, moi, je devrais pouvoir faire traîner les négo.
And I should be able to drag out the negotiations.

160
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,980
De la part de Mathias Barneville ?
On behalf of Mathias Barneville?

161
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:37,820
Merci.
Thank you.

162
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:55,120
Noémie n'est pas là, elle est souffrante.
Noémie isn't in, she's unwell.

163
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,900
Je peux prendre un message ?
Can I take a message?

164
00:05:57,650 --> 00:05:58,150
Très bien.
Very well.

165
00:05:58,770 --> 00:05:59,770
Merci, au revoir.
Thank you, goodbye.

166
00:06:00,950 --> 00:06:02,870
Tu veux pas dire autre chose que souffrante ?
You don't mean anything other than unwell?

167
00:06:02,870 --> 00:06:03,670
C'est glauque.
That's grim.

168
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,690
Ah non, moi, j'adore, ça fait Emma Bovary.
Oh no, I love it — very Emma Bovary.

169
00:06:09,170 --> 00:06:09,490
Camille.
Camille.

170
00:06:10,170 --> 00:06:13,490
Camille, tu peux appeler le directeur de casting du film des Majaks,
Camille, can you call the casting director for the Majaks film,

171
00:06:13,530 --> 00:06:17,290
lui dire que Gérard Lanvin lui envoie ce jeune homme pour le rôle de Bassine.
tell him Gérard Lanvin is sending this young man in for the role of Bassine.

172
00:06:17,490 --> 00:06:19,610
Ouais, euh, je suis un peu sous l'eau, là.
Yeah, uh, I'm a bit swamped right now.

173
00:06:20,430 --> 00:06:20,950
Demandez à lui.
Ask him.

174
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:22,410
Ah non, moi, je peux pas du tout.
Oh no, I really can't.

175
00:06:22,450 --> 00:06:25,250
Faut que je rattrape tout le retard de Gabriel, qui est assez monstrueux, comme vous le savez.
I need to catch up on all of Gabriel's backlog, which is pretty massive, as you know.

176
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,700
Non, mais c'est pas normal que tout soit débordé.
No, but it's not right that everyone's overwhelmed.

177
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,620
T'es sûre que t'es bien organisée, là ?
Are you sure you're well organized?

178
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,620
Ok, c'est bon, je vais le faire.
Ok, fine, I'll do it.

179
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:32,200
Merci.
Thank you.

180
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,340
De quoi vous parliez ? De moi ?
What were you talking about? Me?

181
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:41,870
Non, pas du tout.
No, not at all.

182
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:48,440
Tu peux me sortir l'hystérique des négo, des contrats de Lucchini, Berriand et Léa Seydoux, s'il te plaît ?
Can you pull the hysterical one from the negotiations, the contracts for Lucchini, Berriand and Léa Seydoux, please?

183
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:48,780
Tout de suite.
Right away.

184
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:49,400
Ah, tout de suite.
Ah, right away.

185
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,460
Non, tout de suite.
No, right now.

186
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,220
Moi, je pense qu'elle va avoir un gosse, il range pas sa chambre, il est décapité.
Me, I think she's going to have a kid, he doesn't clean his room, he gets his head cut off.

187
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,560
Excuse-moi, Camille, y a ton conseiller arrivé, là, je dois lui donner quoi ?
Excuse me, Camille, your advisor just arrived — what should I give him?

188
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,210
Déjà, euh, attends.
Hang on, uh, wait.

189
00:07:02,770 --> 00:07:08,580
Ah, ok, voilà, c'est pour Makeover Productions, tu peux le mettre dans une enveloppe, ça...
Ah, okay, right, this is for Makeover Productions, can you put it in an envelope, so...

190
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:09,320
Ça marche.
Got it.

