00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:06,700
Tu vas voir, ça va être incroyable.
You'll see, it's going to be incredible.

383
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,520
Ta vie va changer, Camille.
Your life is going to change, Camille.

384
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,420
Bah, tienne aussi, Camille.
Well, so will yours, Camille.

385
00:15:15,130 --> 00:15:15,870
Allez, là, fonce.
Come on, go for it.

386
00:15:15,870 --> 00:15:17,030
Qu'est-ce que tu fous ?
What are you doing?

387
00:15:17,030 --> 00:15:17,650
Où ça ?
Where?

388
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:19,410
Au casting pour rattraper le coup, enfin.
To the casting to fix things, obviously.

389
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:25,620
Je t'aime.
I love you.

390
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:26,560
Moi aussi.
I love you too.

391
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,240
Donc, voilà, je me présente.
So, here I am, let me introduce myself.

392
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:36,860
J'ai aucune expérience dans le métier.
I have no experience in the industry.

393
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:39,940
Par contre, ce qui est sûr, alors sûr et certain, c'est que depuis tout petit, je sais que je vais être comédien.
But what I do know — know for certain — is that since I was a little kid, I've known I'd be an actor.

394
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:41,880
D'ailleurs, je peux vous raconter une petite anecdote comme ça pour rigoler.
Actually, let me tell you a little anecdote, just for fun.

395
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:42,580
Je sais que ça va vous faire marrer.
I know it'll make you laugh.

396
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:45,320
Le jour de ma naissance, le médecin a lui-même été impressionné par mon charisme.
On the day I was born, the doctor himself was impressed by my charisma.

397
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:47,700
À la naissance.
At birth.

398
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:48,920
Imagine maintenant.
Imagine now.

399
00:15:50,470 --> 00:15:51,190
À mon âge.
At my age.

400
00:15:51,930 --> 00:15:52,690
Deux minutes, deux minutes.
Two minutes, two minutes.

401
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,430
On le voit pour Baptiste, lui ?
Are we seeing him for Baptiste?

402
00:15:56,210 --> 00:15:57,050
C'est une blague.
You're joking.

403
00:15:57,250 --> 00:15:58,850
Je sais, mais c'est une idée de Gérard.
I know, but it was Gérard's idea.

404
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:01,700
Bon.
Right.

405
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:04,560
La taille en chaussures, c'est bien 42, hein ?
Shoe size is 42, correct?

406
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:04,780
Oui.
Yes.

407
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:07,220
8,5 en taille américaine.
8.5 in US sizing.

408
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:08,860
Baisser les bras.
Arms down.

409
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:10,500
101.
101.

410
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,140
Très bien.
Very good.

411
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,540
Je prends la taille et je vous libère.
I'll take your measurement and let you go.

412
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:12,980
Merci.
Thank you.

413
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:20,980
Alors, rentrez pas le ventre.
Now, don't suck in your stomach.

414
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:21,900
Après, le pantalon sert trop.
Otherwise the trousers are too tight.

415
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:22,700
Je rentre pas, là.
I'm not sucking it in.

416
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:23,680
Relâchez.
Relax.

417
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:25,040
Encore.
Again.

418
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:26,140
Très bien.
Very good.

419
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:27,430
94.
94.

420
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:28,230
C'est bon.
That's fine.

421
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:32,510
Ah, ça, c'est n'importe quoi.
Ah, this is absolutely ridiculous.

422
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:34,400
Bon sang.
Good grief.

423
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:38,540
Mathias, le rôle prévu, c'était celui de Bastille, le malade garde du corps.
Mathias, the part we had in mind was Bastille, the sick bodyguard.

424
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:40,440
Il y avait trois répliques, un peu de figure, ça allait très bien.
Three lines, a bit of screen time — it was perfectly fine.

425
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,640
Là, il envisage pour un rôle beaucoup trop gros pour lui.
Now he's going for a role way too big for him.

426
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:44,120
Il n'a jamais rien fait, le monde.
He's never done anything in his life.

427
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:46,260
Il va se planter, et moi, je vais passer pour un con.
He's going to crash and burn, and I'll look like an idiot.

428
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,440
Mais si, c'est moi qui l'ai présenté.
But I'm the one who introduced him.

429
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:51,260
Eh ben, tu me rappelles, hein ?
Well, give me a call, yeah?

430
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:51,920
OK.
OK.

431
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,210
Emma, je peux vous voir deux minutes ?
Emma, can I have a word with you?

432
00:16:56,210 --> 00:16:56,610
Oui, oui.
Yes, of course.

433
00:17:08,370 --> 00:17:11,110
Mais c'est qui, ce phénomène que vous nous avez envoyé, là ?
Who is this character you sent us, anyway?

434
00:17:11,370 --> 00:17:12,190
Justement, je vous explique.
That's exactly what I was going to explain.

435
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:13,290
Il est génial.
He's brilliant.

436
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,560
Génial, c'est-à-dire ?
Brilliant — meaning what, exactly?

437
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:16,840
Alors, c'est pas du tout le personnage.
OK, so he's not the character at all.

438
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:19,220
D'ailleurs, au début, je me suis dit, mais il est complètement fou, ce Gérard.
At first, I thought, what is Gérard thinking, is he completely out of his mind.

439
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:20,260
Mais tu m'étonnes.
Tell me about it.

440
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:21,380
Non, mais après, j'ai compris.
No, but then I understood.

441
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,440
J'ai vu ce que vous avez vu.
I saw what you saw.

442
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,180
Enfin, c'est...
I mean, it's...

443
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,300
Un talent brut, quoi.
Raw talent, you know.

444
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:29,140
Une force explosive, comme ça, et de la sensibilité.
This explosive energy, and real sensitivity too.

445
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:32,080
Ah non, c'est hyper intéressant, vraiment.
No, it's genuinely fascinating.

446
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:34,920
Hyper, tu sais pas, intéressant, c'est ce que je me suis dit.
Fascinating — that's exactly what I thought.

447
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,780
Et c'est qui, son agent ?
And who's his agent?

448
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:37,600
Moi.
Me.

449
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:42,270
Camille Valentini, ASK.
Camille Valentini, ASK.

450
00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:43,110
Enchantée.
Pleased to meet you.

451
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:43,490
Enchantée.
Likewise.

452
00:17:44,670 --> 00:17:45,470
Camille, ça va ?
Camille, how are you?

453
00:17:45,470 --> 00:17:45,810
Ça va.
Fine.

454
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:50,270
Moi, j'ai l'impression qu'il a tout le temps peur de mon jugement.
I feel like he's always afraid of my judgment.

455
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:55,090
Non, c'est vrai, j'ai l'impression que t'as peur de ce que je pourrais penser,
No, really, I feel like you're scared of what I might think,

456
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:56,090
de ce que je pourrais dire.
what I might say.

457
00:17:56,970 --> 00:18:00,510
Surtout après ce qui s'est passé l'an dernier avec Camille, notre séparation,
Especially after what happened last year with Camille, our split,

458
00:18:00,510 --> 00:18:00,750
tout ça.
all of that.

459
00:18:01,430 --> 00:18:04,560
J'ai besoin de vérité, d'intimité.
I need honesty, intimacy.

460
00:18:05,550 --> 00:18:08,230
Et je sais que c'est pas dans ta nature.
And I know that doesn't come naturally to you.

461
00:18:08,870 --> 00:18:10,190
Mais moi, j'ai besoin de communiquer.
But I need to communicate.

462
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:17,360
J'ai besoin de savoir ce qu'il pense et ce qu'il veut.
I need to know what he thinks and what he wants.

463
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:18,100
Voilà.
That's it.

464
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:20,140
J'ai besoin de savoir ce qu'il veut.
I need to know what he wants.

465
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:22,360
Vous le savez, vous, Mathias, ce que vous voulez ?
Do you know what you want, Mathias?

466
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:24,160
Mais qu'il lâche ma joie, au nom de Dieu !
I wish he'd get off my back, for God's sake!

467
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:25,500
Pardon ?
I beg your pardon?

468
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:28,380
Non, pardon, excusez-moi, je...
No, sorry, forgive me, I...

469
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:32,360
Je suis stressé, c'est le travail.
I'm stressed — it's work.

470
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:35,820
Il occupe beaucoup de place dans votre vie, il me semble, le travail, Mathias, non ?
Work seems to take up a lot of space in your life, Mathias, wouldn't you say?

471
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:37,240
Son travail, c'est sa vie.
Work is his life.

472
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:40,360
Mais non, mais non, mais c'est qu'en ce moment, j'ai des rapports compliqués
No, no, it's just that right now I have a complicated relationship

473
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:41,980
avec, avec, avec, avec...
with, with, with, with...

474
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,340
Enfin, avec lui, là.
Well, with him, you know.

475
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,460
Comment est-ce qu'on résiste à un psychopathe ?
How do you stand up to a psychopath?

476
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,400
Vous pouvez peut-être m'expliquer ça, vous.
Maybe you can explain that to me.

477
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:54,060
C'est avec lui que je devrais venir parler ici, tiens. Non ?
He's the one I should be bringing here to talk. Don't you think?

478
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,340
Il me semble qu'il est déjà là. Non ?
It seems to me he's already here. Isn't he?

479
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,900
Tu viens de trouver des bureaux canons sur le bon coin. On se prend rendez-vous ?
You just found some great offices on Le Bon Coin. Shall we book a time?

480
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,880
Et tu leur dis pas nos vrais noms ?
And you're not giving them our real names?

481
00:19:10,930 --> 00:19:11,410
Evidemment, patate.
Obviously, dummy.

482
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:13,650
Non, mais te fous pas de ma gueule, parce que là, là, c'est suffisamment la merde comme ça.
No, don't take the piss, because right now, right now, it's already enough of a mess.

483
00:19:13,750 --> 00:19:17,250
J'ai Jean-Paul Besse dans mon bureau, il a décidé qu'il fallait boucler aujourd'hui la négo pour le prochain film de Norman.
I've got Jean-Paul Besse in my office, he's decided we need to close the deal today on Norman's next film.

484
00:19:17,550 --> 00:19:20,590
Sauf que moi, ça fait deux mois que je lui cours après, et là, il est pressé. Je fais quoi ?
Except I've been chasing him for two months, and now he's in a rush. What do I do?

485
00:19:20,590 --> 00:19:22,330
Merde. Bah, tu négocies au plus bas, c'est tout.
Damn. Well, you negotiate low, that's all.

486
00:19:22,530 --> 00:19:25,060
Ah, je négocie au plus bas. Ok, ça va. Théa, c'est...
Right, I negotiate low. Ok, fine. Théa, it's...

487
00:19:26,210 --> 00:19:27,850
Je pense que j'ai trouvé un truc pour repousser la signature.
I think I found something to push back the signing.

488
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:28,830
Super, ça va.
Great, good.

489
00:19:29,210 --> 00:19:30,990
Oh ! Qu'est-ce qu'il... Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ? Merde !
Oh! What's he... What's going on? Damn!

490
00:19:32,230 --> 00:19:33,530
Pourquoi tu chuchotes ?
Why are you whispering?

491
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:34,800
Hop.
There we go.

492
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:37,440
Parce que je suis... J'ai fait enrouer... Voilà.
Because I'm... I've gone hoarse... That's why.

493
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:40,920
Gabriel.
Gabriel.

494
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,040
Excuse-moi, Jean-Paul.
Excuse me, Jean-Paul.

495
00:19:46,390 --> 00:19:48,910
Bon, pour le contrat de Norman, j'ai bien réfléchi.
So, about Norman's contract, I've given it some thought.

496
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:53,590
C'est vrai que... J'ai bien compris, hein. C'est difficile de faire du cinéma en ce moment.
I understand, I really do. It's tough to make films right now.

497
00:19:53,790 --> 00:19:54,470
Ça, c'est très dur.
It really is.

498
00:19:54,730 --> 00:19:59,290
Bon, financer un film, c'est l'enfer. Les producteurs, vous tirez la langue.
Financing a movie is a nightmare. You producers are stretched thin.

499
00:20:00,310 --> 00:20:03,750
Evidemment, on va pas vous prendre... On va rester humain.
Of course, we're not going to squeeze you... We'll stay reasonable.

500
00:20:03,910 --> 00:20:07,470
Oui. Par contre, on a un gros problème avec cette histoire de produits dérivés.
Yes. However, we have a big problem with this whole merchandising situation.

501
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:09,560
Bah, parce que pour nous, c'est un problème.
Because for us, it's an issue.

502
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:11,580
C'est impossible que la tête de Léa Seydoux se retrouve sur des slips.
There's no way Léa Seydoux's face ends up on underwear.

503
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:16,900
Donc, il me faut la liste détaillée et exhaustive de tous les produits dérivés où peut apparaître Léa.
So I need a detailed, exhaustive list of every piece of merchandise Léa could appear on.

504
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:20,800
Avec leur taille, leur composition, le lieu de fabrication.
With sizes, materials, and place of manufacture.

505
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:23,280
Là, on est très à cheval sur les principes.
We're very firm on our principles here.

506
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:29,720
Donc, ça veut dire pas de test sur les animaux, pas d'OGM, empreinte écologique réduite, transport en circuit court.
So that means no animal testing, no GMOs, minimal carbon footprint, short-circuit transport.

507
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:32,560
Et évidemment, pas de travail des enfants.
And obviously, no child labor.

508
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:37,400
L'idée, c'est de rester sur la négo prévue, hein.
The idea is to stick to the original deal, right.

509
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,300
Un peu basse, certes.
A bit low, granted.

510
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:40,140
Mais juste pour cette fois.
But just this once.

511
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,320
Et on travaille en bonne intelligence.
And we work together in good faith.

512
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,160
Hein ?
Right?

513
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:44,040
Bah, écoute, c'est parfait.
Well, look, that's perfect.

514
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,760
Si seulement tous les agents étaient comme toi.
If only all agents were like you.

515
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:46,380
Bonjour.
Hello.

516
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:47,880
Michel Janowski.
Michel Janowski.

517
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:49,040
Enchanté, enchanté, vraiment.
Delighted, truly delighted.

518
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:50,200
Bon, bah, je vous laisse.
Well, I'll leave you to it.

519
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:50,820
Nous, on avait fini.
We were done anyway.

520
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:51,840
Salut.
Bye.

521
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,060
Non, peut-être pas.
Maybe not quite.

522
00:20:54,370 --> 00:20:56,610
Norman, il fait combien de vues déjà sur YouTube ?
How many views does Norman get on YouTube again?

523
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:58,070
Bah, ça dépend.
Well, it depends.

524
00:20:58,230 --> 00:20:59,850
Enfin, c'est... c'est inégal, hein.
I mean, it's... it's inconsistent, you know.

525
00:20:59,930 --> 00:21:00,870
Entre 9 et 10 millions.
Between 9 and 10 million.

526
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:04,020
Et le film d'Odiard dans lequel il a joué, combien d'entrées ?
And the Odiard film he was in — how many tickets sold?

527
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,080
Non, mais ça, ça veut rien dire.
No, but that doesn't mean anything.

528
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:07,020
2,5 millions.
2.5 million.

529
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,020
Donc, on va reprendre la discussion tranquillement.
So we're going to restart this discussion calmly.

530
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:23,020
Qu'est-ce qui s'est passé avec ce type aux essais, là ?
What happened with that guy at the auditions?

531
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:24,420
Pourquoi tu m'as pas répondu au téléphone ?
Why didn't you answer my call?

532
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:26,180
J'ai eu un petit cafouillage, j'ai eu.
I had a little mix-up, I did.

533
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,560
Un petit cafouillage ? Non, mais tu te fous de moi ?
A little mix-up? Are you kidding me?

534
00:21:28,560 --> 00:21:30,880
Lanvin et tes furions, on a l'air de quoi, là, maintenant ?
Lanvin and your lot — what do we look like right now?

535
00:21:31,690 --> 00:21:34,550
Ah bah, on a l'air de ceux qui viennent de recruter la future petite bombe du cinéma français.
We look like the people who just signed the next big thing in French cinema.

536
00:21:36,270 --> 00:21:38,290
Samy a cartonné ses essais et veulent l'envoi en call-back demain.
Samy nailed his audition and they want him for a callback tomorrow.

537
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:40,490
Eh oui, maintenant, c'est moi son agent.
And yes, now I'm his agent.

538
00:21:47,350 --> 00:21:50,290
Rappelle, je t'ai vu, depuis que je suis à bord, même tes gaffes se transforment en succès.
Think about it — ever since I came on board, even your screw-ups turn into wins.

539
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:54,500
Ah, Camille Valentini.
Ah, Camille Valentini.

540
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,140
L'agent double.
The double agent.

541
00:21:58,090 --> 00:21:58,910
Est-ce que t'es prêt ?
You ready?

542
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:00,480
Deux.
Two.

543
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:01,180
Attention.
Heads up.

544
00:22:02,270 --> 00:22:02,770
Accroche-toi.
Hold on tight.

545
00:22:04,550 --> 00:22:05,130
Eh ouais.
Oh yeah.

546
00:22:05,870 --> 00:22:07,770
Les téléphones de la nouvelle Camille Valentini.
The phones for the new Camille Valentini.

547
00:22:08,210 --> 00:22:08,990
Un seul numéro.
One number only.

548
00:22:09,510 --> 00:22:11,810
Et une messagerie avec voix électronique.
And a voicemail with an electronic voice.

549
00:22:12,150 --> 00:22:13,270
Un pour toi, un pour moi.
One for you, one for me.

550
00:22:13,590 --> 00:22:14,930
Mais c'est génial !
This is genius!

551
00:22:14,930 --> 00:22:15,630
Bah oui !
Right?!

552
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:17,910
Bah, tu vas voir, moi, j'ai pas le choix, mais non plus.
Well, you'll see, I don't have a choice, and neither do you.

553
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:21,280
Alors, j'ai créé une adresse mail commune.
So I created a shared email address.

554
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:21,720
OK.
OK.

555
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:24,800
Et là, on met tout sur la box avec un fichier par talent.
And here, we put everything on the drive with a file per talent.

556
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,100
Les miens en rouge, les tiens en vert.
Mine in red, yours in green.

557
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:31,180
Là, on note tous les castings en cours pour bien savoir qui est qui.
Here, we list all the ongoing castings so we know exactly who's who.

558
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:32,020
Qui envoie quel acteur.
Who's sending which actor.

559
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:36,220
Et là, enfin, bah, le calendrier où on note tout ce qu'on va voir au théâtre,
And here, finally, the calendar where we log everything we're going to see — theatre,

560
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:38,420
one-man show, avant-première, etc., etc.
one-man shows, premieres, etc., etc.

