00:29:47,230 --> 00:29:48,430
J'ai plein de dossiers en retard.
I've got a pile of overdue files.

747
00:29:48,770 --> 00:29:50,150
Il faut que je réponde à 12 000 mails.
I need to answer 12,000 emails.

748
00:29:50,530 --> 00:29:51,950
Il va falloir patienter, Mathias.
You'll have to be patient, Mathias.

749
00:29:52,870 --> 00:29:53,490
Ah bon ?
Oh really?

750
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:56,460
Eh bien, ben écoutez, quand vous pourrez.
Well, alright, whenever you can.

751
00:29:56,940 --> 00:30:05,100
T'as balzé, Mathias ?
Did you get laid, Mathias?

752
00:30:05,100 --> 00:30:09,010
Le pouvoir du corset, quoi.
The power of the corset, eh.

753
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:13,240
Vous êtes prêts ?
Are you ready?

754
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:13,900
Excusez-moi.
Excuse me.

755
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:16,700
Par contre, on commence à partir du moment où je me prends la balle.
We start from the moment I take the bullet, though.

756
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:18,080
Euh...
Uh...

757
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:20,920
Ben non, non, non, après, je voudrais pas que tu te fasses mal en tombant, là.
No, no, no, after — I don't want you hurting yourself falling down.

758
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:21,820
Ah non, mais vous en faites pas.
Oh no, don't worry about that.

759
00:30:21,880 --> 00:30:22,680
Moi, j'ai fait 12 ans de judo.
I've done 12 years of judo.

760
00:30:22,700 --> 00:30:23,320
Je suis incassable.
I'm unbreakable.

761
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:24,260
Bon, OK.
Alright, OK.

762
00:30:24,940 --> 00:30:25,520
Allez, on y va.
Come on, let's go.

763
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:28,460
C'est bon ?
Good?

764
00:30:28,460 --> 00:30:28,920
Ça tourne.
Rolling.

765
00:30:34,420 --> 00:30:34,660
Super.
Great.

766
00:30:34,980 --> 00:30:35,700
T'es prêt ?
You ready?

767
00:30:35,700 --> 00:30:35,920
Ouais.
Yeah.

768
00:30:36,220 --> 00:30:36,860
Allez, c'est parti.
Alright, here we go.

769
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:47,680
Je t'incruste à l'île de chez ma mère, comme d'habitude.
I'll plant you on the island at my mom's place, as usual.

770
00:30:50,170 --> 00:30:50,650
C'est un...
It's a...

771
00:30:50,900 --> 00:30:51,340
Parle comme ça.
Talk like that.

772
00:30:52,180 --> 00:30:53,220
Fonds, je t'ai dit, je vais me cacher derrière.
Blend in, I told you — I'll hide behind you.

773
00:30:53,300 --> 00:30:53,760
Ils me verront pas.
They won't see me.

774
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:55,620
Et tu crois que je vais te laisser là, tout seul ?
And you think I'm going to leave you there all alone?

775
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:56,120
Allez, viens, aide-moi.
Come on, help me out.

776
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:56,660
Allez, viens.
Come on.

777
00:30:56,720 --> 00:30:56,900
Allez.
Let's go.

778
00:30:59,270 --> 00:31:00,030
C'est vrai, Gérard ?
Is that true, Gérard?

779
00:31:00,650 --> 00:31:01,430
Mais non !
Of course not!

780
00:31:02,410 --> 00:31:03,110
Oh, putain !
Oh, damn!

781
00:31:04,310 --> 00:31:05,450
Ah, je me suis baissé le dos.
Ah, I threw out my back.

782
00:31:05,450 --> 00:31:06,830
Je suis désolé, Gérard.
I'm sorry, Gérard.

783
00:31:07,390 --> 00:31:08,530
Il fallait m'aider, putain.
You should've helped me, damn it.

784
00:31:09,110 --> 00:31:14,690
En même temps, si c'était Franck qui était blessé...
Then again, if it were Franck who was injured...

785
00:31:17,250 --> 00:31:20,690
C'est un mec qui a des failles énormes sous ses airs de sauveur ultra-viril.
He's a guy with massive flaws beneath that ultra-macho savior act.

786
00:31:20,710 --> 00:31:23,640
Et s'il était blessé, à ce moment-là de l'histoire,
And if he were injured, at that point in the story,

787
00:31:23,740 --> 00:31:25,980
ça l'obligerait à baisser la garde devant Baptiste.
it would force him to let his guard down around Baptiste.

788
00:31:26,420 --> 00:31:28,130
Ça serait beau, ça.
That would be beautiful.

789
00:31:28,270 --> 00:31:28,910
Ah ouais, mais carrément.
Oh yeah, absolutely.

790
00:31:28,990 --> 00:31:30,110
Mais carrément de rien du tout.
Absolutely nothing at all.

791
00:31:30,890 --> 00:31:33,370
On va s'en tenir à ce qui a été écrit, lu, signé, approuvé.
We're sticking to what was written, read, signed, approved.

792
00:31:33,510 --> 00:31:34,730
Voilà, c'est Franck qui est de Baptiste.
Right, so Franck is Baptiste's guy.

793
00:31:34,870 --> 00:31:36,450
Et Franck, il a pas besoin qu'on le porte.
And Franck doesn't need to be carried.

794
00:31:36,750 --> 00:31:39,370
Si, si, si, parce que s'il est blessé, je vous assure, Gérard,
Yes, yes, yes, because if he's injured, I'm telling you, Gérard,

795
00:31:39,430 --> 00:31:40,450
ça donne à la scène...
it gives the scene...

796
00:31:41,210 --> 00:31:43,090
un caractère sacrificiel, ça fait biblique.
a sacrificial quality, it feels biblical.

797
00:31:43,270 --> 00:31:44,770
Et du coup, ça fait un vrai tandem.
And that makes for a real duo.

798
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:47,110
Plutôt qu'un héros solitaire, comme on a déjà vu tout le temps.
Rather than a lone hero, like we've seen a thousand times.

799
00:31:47,250 --> 00:31:47,910
Oui, oui, exactement.
Yes, yes, exactly.

800
00:31:48,530 --> 00:31:48,810
Carrément.
Absolutely.

801
00:31:48,870 --> 00:31:49,890
Mais arrête avec les carréments.
Stop with the "absolutely"s.

802
00:31:50,470 --> 00:31:51,830
On va pas tout changer en cinq minutes.
We're not changing everything in five minutes.

803
00:31:52,510 --> 00:31:53,550
On arrête les conneries, là.
Enough with the nonsense, now.

804
00:31:53,730 --> 00:31:54,910
Sinon, ça va pas le faire avec moi.
Otherwise, it's not going to work out with me.

805
00:31:55,770 --> 00:31:56,570
D'accord ?
Understood?

806
00:31:56,570 --> 00:32:01,860
Ça peut plus marcher, moi, putain.
This just can't work anymore, damn it.

807
00:32:02,620 --> 00:32:03,520
Mais Gérard...
But Gérard...

808
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:05,100
C'est naze, hein, votre truc, là.
Your thing is rubbish, you know that.

809
00:32:06,170 --> 00:32:07,950
Désolé pour le ménage, je viens juste de le rentrer.
Sorry about the mess, I just brought it in.

810
00:32:09,030 --> 00:32:09,830
C'est pas un problème.
It's no problem.

811
00:32:10,010 --> 00:32:12,630
Vous savez, j'ai l'habitude de voir le potentiel au-delà des apparences.
You know, I'm used to seeing potential beyond appearances.

812
00:32:12,770 --> 00:32:13,950
Je fais ça toute la journée.
It's what I do all day.

813
00:32:13,950 --> 00:32:15,510
Vous êtes décoratrice intérieure ?
You're an interior decorator?

814
00:32:15,510 --> 00:32:17,090
Tout à fait.
That's right.

815
00:32:23,130 --> 00:32:24,350
Je vous conseille de pas traîner.
I'd advise you not to wait too long.

816
00:32:25,540 --> 00:32:27,420
Il y a un gros turnover de bureaux, en ce moment.
There's a big turnover in office space right now.

817
00:32:28,020 --> 00:32:29,620
Avec toutes les entreprises qui se cassent la figure.
With all the companies going under.

818
00:32:30,220 --> 00:32:32,470
C'est bien, hein ?
Nice, right?

819
00:32:32,470 --> 00:32:32,910
Ouais.
Yeah.

820
00:32:33,250 --> 00:32:34,450
Vous voyez aussi, il est bien.
You see, this one's good too.

821
00:32:35,090 --> 00:32:37,030
Gabriel, on va pas recevoir nos talents dans une chambre de bonne.
Gabriel, we can't be meeting with our talent in a studio flat.

822
00:32:37,170 --> 00:32:37,430
Bien sûr.
Of course.

823
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:41,540
Ah !
Oh!

824
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:44,360
Qu'est-ce que vous faites ici ?
What are you doing here?

825
00:32:45,560 --> 00:32:45,880
Euh...
Uh...

826
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:46,760
Ben...
Well...

827
00:32:47,240 --> 00:32:48,580
On visite un appartement.
We're looking at an apartment.

828
00:32:48,980 --> 00:32:50,560
La famille, ça grandit, hein ?
The family's growing, huh?

829
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:52,980
C'est toi, le papa ?
Are you the dad?

830
00:32:52,980 --> 00:32:54,600
Ah non, Lola, non, non, non, Guy, pas du tout.
Oh no, Lola, no, no, no, Guy, not at all.

831
00:32:54,660 --> 00:32:54,940
Non, je...
No, I...

832
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,500
Je voulais lui donner mon avis amical.
I just wanted to give him my friendly opinion.

833
00:32:56,720 --> 00:32:59,460
Parce qu'il paraît que je suis très doué pour sentir l'âme des lieux, alors...
Because apparently I have a great sense for the soul of a place, so...

834
00:32:59,460 --> 00:33:01,220
C'est marrant de vous voir ici.
It's funny running into you here.

835
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:06,260
Paris est tout petit pour ceux qui, comme nous, s'aiment d'un aussi grand amour.
Paris is very small for those of us who, like us, share such a great love.

836
00:33:07,420 --> 00:33:09,180
Désolée, la serrure est un peu retorce.
Sorry, the lock is a bit tricky.

837
00:33:09,940 --> 00:33:10,580
Bonjour, monsieur.
Good day, sir.

838
00:33:12,090 --> 00:33:13,810
Voilà, alors, je vous laisse la fiche du local.
Right then, I'll leave you the property sheet.

839
00:33:14,090 --> 00:33:15,230
Merci, on vous rappelle, hein ?
Thanks, we'll be in touch, yeah?

840
00:33:15,230 --> 00:33:16,210
À votre service.
At your service.

841
00:33:16,490 --> 00:33:17,450
Monsieur Giscard ?
Mr. Giscard?

842
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:19,160
Madame Giscard ?
Mrs. Giscard?

843
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:19,540
Ah !
Ah!

844
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:23,460
C'est une private joke.
It's an inside joke.

845
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:26,860
Bon, ben, je vous laisse.
Right, well, I'll leave you to it.

846
00:33:27,930 --> 00:33:28,410
Au repos.
At ease.

847
00:33:29,010 --> 00:33:29,050
Ah !
Ah!

848
00:33:29,450 --> 00:33:29,690
Oui.
Yes.

849
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:36,880
Ben oui, trente ans de béhérite.
Well yeah, thirty years in the business.

850
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:37,600
C'est pas une truffe, le mec.
The guy's no amateur.

851
00:33:37,700 --> 00:33:39,360
Il peut pas finir porté sur le lot d'un débutant.
He can't end up on some rookie's reel.

852
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:39,940
C'est grotesque.
It's absurd.

853
00:33:40,020 --> 00:33:40,780
Ben, attends, c'est pas fait.
Well, hang on, it's not done yet.

854
00:33:40,860 --> 00:33:43,280
Quand Emma va mettre son lit dans le scénario et qu'elle va se rendre compte des changements
When Emma puts her heart into the script and realizes what kind of changes

855
00:33:43,280 --> 00:33:44,040
que ça représente...
that means...

856
00:33:44,040 --> 00:33:46,180
Oui, ben, elle pourra toujours demander à ta fille de lui filer un coup de main.
Yeah, well, she can always ask your daughter to give her a hand.

857
00:33:46,240 --> 00:33:47,060
Elle est scénariste, apparemment.
She's a screenwriter, apparently.

858
00:33:47,260 --> 00:33:48,020
Écoute, je suis désolé.
Look, I'm sorry.

859
00:33:48,100 --> 00:33:48,640
Elle débute.
She's just starting out.

860
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:49,420
Elle a voulu en faire trop.
She tried to bite off more than she could chew.

861
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:50,840
Mais ils veulent tous en faire trop.
But they all do.

862
00:33:51,340 --> 00:33:53,880
Tu verrais les filles, là, quand ils arrivent, frétillées du berlingot.
You should see the girls when they show up, all bright-eyed and bushy-tailed.

863
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:54,680
C'est un délice.
It's delightful.

864
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:58,260
Et Emma, elle, quand elle le voit, elle a la tête qui se remplit d'eau.
And Emma, when she sees him, her head just goes blank.

865
00:33:58,340 --> 00:33:59,300
Elle est en apnée, la gonzesse.
She's completely underwater, that one.

866
00:33:59,460 --> 00:34:00,300
Il y a plus de taulier.
There's no one in charge anymore.

867
00:34:00,420 --> 00:34:01,220
Il y a plus de patron.
There's no boss anymore.

868
00:34:01,360 --> 00:34:01,960
C'est flippant.
It's unsettling.

869
00:34:02,100 --> 00:34:03,360
Écoute, Samy, il est pas encore engagé.
Look, Samy isn't signed on yet.

870
00:34:03,380 --> 00:34:04,180
T'as ton mot à dire, tu sais.
You have a say in this, you know.

871
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:05,700
C'est quand même toi, la vedette, Gérard.
You're the star, after all, Gérard.

872
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:07,020
Moi, j'ai juste voulu aider.
I just wanted to help.

873
00:34:07,380 --> 00:34:08,880
Et je me suis mis dans la merde tout seul, voilà.
And I got myself into this mess all on my own, that's all.

874
00:34:09,100 --> 00:34:09,820
Je suis marron, maintenant.
I'm stuck now.

875
00:34:09,900 --> 00:34:10,740
Qu'est-ce que tu veux que je fasse ?
What do you want me to do?

876
00:34:10,740 --> 00:34:12,560
Que je le prive de la chance de sa vie, ce môme ?
Deprive the kid of the chance of a lifetime?

877
00:34:12,560 --> 00:34:13,460
Je peux pas faire ça.
I can't do that.

878
00:34:14,530 --> 00:34:17,990
Vu l'énergumène, il en aura d'autres, des chances, dans sa vie.
Knowing that guy, he'll have plenty of other chances in his life.

879
00:34:19,420 --> 00:34:20,980
Casser le cliché, c'est devenu un cliché.
Subverting the cliché has become a cliché itself.

880
00:34:21,020 --> 00:34:21,560
Tout le monde fait ça.
Everyone does it.

881
00:34:22,260 --> 00:34:23,760
Donc, Samy, c'est l'inverse du personnage.
So Samy is the opposite of the character.

882
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:24,360
Vous le savez bien.
You know that perfectly well.

883
00:34:24,680 --> 00:34:26,780
Donc, avant d'avoir un contre-emploi, ils ont déjà un emploi.
So before they even play against type, they already have a type.

884
00:34:26,980 --> 00:34:29,320
Oui, mais moi, je pense qu'il va nous surprendre.
Yes, but I think he's going to surprise us.

885
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:29,840
Vraiment.
Really.

886
00:34:30,220 --> 00:34:32,080
Vous savez qu'il peut faire ses cascades lui-même ?
Did you know he can do his own stunts?

887
00:34:32,080 --> 00:34:32,680
Sans blague.
You're kidding.

888
00:34:32,820 --> 00:34:34,200
Elle va être contente, les assurances.
The insurance companies are going to love that.

889
00:34:35,700 --> 00:34:38,420
Mais, Gérard, vous avez un problème avec lui ou...
But Gérard, do you have a problem with him, or...

890
00:34:39,020 --> 00:34:40,120
Dites-moi, hein, si c'est le cas.
Tell me if that's the case.

891
00:34:40,220 --> 00:34:40,960
Pas du tout.
Not at all.

892
00:34:42,590 --> 00:34:43,590
L'homme et la femme de ma vie.
The man and woman of my life.

893
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:45,200
Vous allez bien ?
Are you doing well?

894
00:34:45,200 --> 00:34:45,960
Ça va mieux.
Better now.

895
00:34:46,100 --> 00:34:47,100
Ouais, je suis désolé pour tout à l'heure.
Yeah, I'm sorry about earlier.

896
00:34:47,780 --> 00:34:49,020
Vous êtes venu me filer la réplique ?
You came to run lines with me?

897
00:34:50,390 --> 00:34:51,830
C'est mes derniers essais et...
These are my final screen tests and...

898
00:34:52,630 --> 00:34:53,930
Vous êtes un port de bonheur pour moi, Gérard.
You're good luck for me, Gérard.

899
00:34:54,330 --> 00:34:56,210
Non, je pense que Gérard a d'autres choses à faire, là.
No, I think Gérard has other things to do right now.

900
00:34:56,550 --> 00:34:57,350
Ouais, pas de problème.
Yeah, no problem.

901
00:34:57,450 --> 00:34:58,230
Je vais me débrouiller tout seul.
I'll manage on my own.

902
00:34:58,330 --> 00:34:59,190
De toute façon, j'ai appris toutes les répliques.
Besides, I've learned all the lines.

903
00:34:59,270 --> 00:34:59,970
Je connais le scénario par le cœur.
I know the script by heart.

904
00:35:00,170 --> 00:35:01,130
Au pire, je peux même jouer les deux rôles.
Worst case, I can even play both parts.

905
00:35:01,130 --> 00:35:01,510
Y a pas de problème.
No problem.

906
00:35:03,070 --> 00:35:04,430
Ben, je vais te la donner, la réplique.
Right, I'll feed you the line.

907
00:35:04,830 --> 00:35:05,370
C'est mieux.
Better.

908
00:35:05,630 --> 00:35:05,870
Super.
Great.

909
00:35:06,910 --> 00:35:07,390
Merci, Gérard.
Thanks, Gérard.

910
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:22,680
Regardez.
Look.

911
00:35:25,180 --> 00:35:26,140
C'est quoi, ça ?
What's that?

912
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:29,800
Euh...
Uh...

913
00:35:30,340 --> 00:35:32,560
Eh ben, c'est un site de rencontre, non ?
Well, it's a dating site, isn't it?

914
00:35:33,240 --> 00:35:34,720
Pourquoi j'ai ça dans mon téléphone, moi ?
Why do I have that on my phone?

915
00:35:35,650 --> 00:35:36,430
Je sais rien, moi.
I have no idea.

916
00:35:36,430 --> 00:35:37,670
Peut-être parce que t'es célibataire.
Maybe because you're single.

917
00:35:38,210 --> 00:35:40,550
Peut-être parce que parfois tu fais des choses, après, tu oublies que tu les as faites.
Maybe because sometimes you do things and then forget you did them.

918
00:35:41,150 --> 00:35:42,310
Ben, n'importe quoi.
Oh, come on.

919
00:35:42,350 --> 00:35:43,870
J'ai jamais utilisé ce genre de truc, moi.
I've never used that kind of thing.

920
00:35:44,130 --> 00:35:45,470
Peut-être que tu l'as fait inconsciemment.
Maybe you did it without thinking.

921
00:35:47,310 --> 00:35:47,930
Non, mais arrête, là.
No, knock it off.

922
00:35:47,950 --> 00:35:50,330
Je vois bien que t'as ton regard de quand t'essayes de m'enfumer, là.
I can see that look you get when you're trying to pull one over on me.

923
00:35:51,370 --> 00:35:51,630
Regarde.
Look.

924
00:35:52,500 --> 00:35:53,440
T'as plein de likes.
You've got loads of likes.

925
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:01,080
Cette petite colombe toute choupinoupinou, là.
This cute little dove right here.

926
00:36:01,940 --> 00:36:02,880
Regarde, t'as même un cœur.
Look, you even got a heart.

927
00:36:03,660 --> 00:36:04,180
C'est bon.
Alright.

928
00:36:04,280 --> 00:36:04,620
C'est bon.
Alright.

929
00:36:04,680 --> 00:36:05,540
Je vais me débrouiller.
I'll manage.

930
00:36:06,380 --> 00:36:06,640
Merci.
Thanks.

931
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:07,540
Tu peux y aller.
You can go.

932
00:36:07,780 --> 00:36:07,960
Ouais.
Yeah.

933
00:36:09,650 --> 00:36:11,270
De toute façon, c'est ce que tu voulais, non ?
That's what you wanted anyway, isn't it?

934
00:36:11,270 --> 00:36:11,630
C'est...
